    <name>
      <text>Calculating exact Values of Trigonometric Ratios for Negative Angles</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Evaluate the following expression exactly:</p>

<p>
\(\sin({@ang1@}^\circ)+\cos({@ang2@}^\circ)\)
</p>

<p>Give your answer in its simplest exact form.</p>

<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p>To evaluate this expression, use the properties of trigonometric functions for negative angles and the exact values of trigonometric ratios.</p>

<p>Recall that sine is an odd function and cosine is an even function:</p>

<p>\(\sin(-\theta)=-\sin(\theta)\)</p>

<p>\(\cos(-\theta)=\cos(\theta)\)</p>

<p>Use these identities to rewrite the expression in terms of positive angles. Then use the reference angles and the signs of the trigonometric ratios to determine the exact values.</p>

<p>Finally, combine the two terms and simplify your answer.</p>

<p>The correct exact answer is \({@ta@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
